  },
  {
   "oldText": "1. Use only the current instance's grid, demos, feedback, and counters; treat instances as independent and do not inspect other task artifacts. Identify the transformation by comparing every input/output cell, dimensions, preserved regions, and changed cells. Follow `arc-divider-recolor` for divider-panel tasks and `arc-rectangle-noise` for rectangular frames/fields. An unchanged demo constrains only that example; it does not establish the general rule or prove the test is unchanged. If the test lacks an apparent divider or other defining structure seen in demos, do not force it into that task family or guess a split; request a demo to establish how the transformation applies.\n",
   "newText": "1. Use only the current instance's grid, demos, feedback, and counters; treat instances as independent and do not inspect other task artifacts. Compare every input/output cell, dimensions, preserved regions, and changed cells. For divider-panel tasks, use `arc-divider-recolor`; for rectangular frames or fields, use `arc-rectangle-noise`. An unchanged demo constrains only that example; it does not establish the general rule or prove the test is unchanged. If the test lacks a defining structure seen in demos, do not force it into that family or guess a split; request a demo to establish applicability.\n"
